A||N||1||Zorba||How much brake pedal travel?||||5||
Z||000000||Zorba||12-15-2000||12:01 PM||||what is your brake <B>pedal travel</B> with the engine running? <P>When I depress my brake, it feels like it travels 1" then it grabs. I must have air in my lines. I would like to brake a bit better with all new rotors and calipers all the way around.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Wm34640.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||12-15-2000||12:37 PM||||After the 1" of travel and it grabs does it feel spongy?  If the pedal is hard once it grabs then it is not likely that you have air in the system.<P>Does your parking brake work?  If not then the rear caliper piston is probably not adjusted properly.  Periodic operation of the parking brake keeps the slack out of the system by keeping the rear caliper pistons adjusted close to contact.  This way they have very little travel before they grab.<P>Actually 1" of pedal travel does not seem excessive to me.<P>Take care,<P>Carroll<P>||||reg||1
